Hey folks,

I recently got an unexpectedly big delivery of AlphaServer DS20 machines
(while I expected something like an alpha station DS10). The machines were
not quite in working order - I'm trying to puzzle them back into shape,
but they are confusing beasts. Maybe someone here has a similar working
machine and can give some hints?

First thing is SCSI confusion. They have an "internal" StorageWorks shelf,
connected apparently via scsi over a small repeater. The cable from the 
repeater was not connected. The connector is a bit strange, but the mainboard
has two matching jacks labeled SCSI bus A and SCSI bus B. So I connected it
to scsi a, but it does not show up anywhere. The schematics on the downside
of the top cover seems to imply that it should run to some pci card - which
I don't have.

I aquired a usable single channel scsi card and connected the other scsi
cable (with standard 50 pin connector) to it, and this makes the CD drive
show up in firmware.

I also have a card that apparently should connect to an extern storage works
shelf (which I also have), but this is not seen by firmware either.

I added a few pci network cards, just for testing (and maybe mounting
root on nfs while I can't get a disk working).

