Is the DEC "miscellaneous network" device the external storage works
connector card? I can not find any traces of USB, so I guess that is an
error in the pcidevs of that (slightly old) NetBSD version and it actually
is the CONTAQ 82C693 PCI-ISA Bridge.

I guess I should continue hunting for the "right" scsi pci card which can
connect both the storage works repeater and the CD drives scsi bus, or add
another internal scsi disk at the first bus behind the CD drive (there is
space and connectors left).

Can I use some kind of adapter to connect the scsi repeater to a stock
